    {
      "id": "TP-038",
      "startMilliseconds": 423670,
      "endMilliseconds": 434670,
      "kind": "fact",
      "text": "A function call is itself an ordinary instruction, and the processor understands it exactly like any other instruction, so it jumps to the first instruction of B and runs B's three instructions in order.",
