    {
      "id": "TP-039",
      "startMilliseconds": 434670,
      "endMilliseconds": 443560,
      "kind": "explanation",
      "text": "The third instruction of B calls function F, so the processor jumps to F's first instruction and runs it, and when F's instruction list is exhausted it returns to the point inside B where F was called.",
